---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import bioImage from '../assets/pixel-art-kevin-db.webp'
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Link from '../components/Link.astro'

import { getEntry } from 'astro:content'

const entry = await getEntry('authors', 'kevin')
if (!entry) throw new Error('Author not found')
const {
  data: { socials },
} = entry
---

<Layout
  title="About | Kevin De Baerdemaeker"
  description="Hi, I'm Kevin De Baerdemaeker, senior software developer in Netflix's games division in Finland, poking at graphics programming, Nix and game dev."
>
  <Image
    class="-mr-4 -mt-4 sm:mt-2 w-24 h-24 sm:w-56 sm:h-56 float-right [transform:rotateY(180deg)]"
    src={bioImage}
    alt=""
    width={320}
    loading="eager"
  />
  <h1 class="text-4xl">Hi, I'm Kevin De Baerdemaeker</h1>
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl">Say hi</h2>
    <ul class="list-[square] list-inside">
      <li>Send me an <Link href={socials.email}>email</Link>.</li>
      <!-- prettier-ignore -->
      <li>Peek at my code on <Link href={socials.github}>GitHub</Link>.</li>
      <!-- prettier-ignore -->
      <li>Or <Link href={socials.linkedin}>LinkedIn</Link>, if that's more your thing.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl">The long version</h2>
    <p>
      I'm a 90s kid who grew up in Belgium. I remember playing

      <!-- prettier-ignore -->
      <Link href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paperboy_(video_game)">Paper Boy</Link>

      on the Commodore 64 when I was a kid, and gaming has always been a part of
      my life. Aside from being glued to a screen, I've spent too much time
      playing with Legos and loved football.
    </p>
    <p>
      I never thought I'd become a programmer, let alone understand how the
      games I played were made. Then a robotics class in Ghent tricked me into
      coding, and I fell down the web rabbit hole: HTML, CSS, JavaScript,
      TypeScript, Node.js, the works.
    </p>
    <p>
      I spent about five years building websites and web apps for folks like
      <Link href="https://freebility.be">Freebility</Link>,
      <Link href="https://famoco.com">Famoco</Link> and
      <Link href="https://epicgames.com">Epic Games</Link>. These days I live in
      Finland and work as a senior software developer in the games division at
      <Link href="https://www.netflix.com">Netflix</Link>. Turns out I get to
      help make them now. I like being all over the stack, from pixel pushing to
      making it go fast, and keeping it all as simple as I can get away with.
    </p>
    <p>
      My brain is chaotic, which is pretty much why this site exists. The
      polished bits end up in my <Link href="/posts/">writing</Link>, the messy
      ones get dumped in my <Link href="/braindump/">notes</Link> and the shiny toys
      land in the <Link href="/lab/">lab</Link>. Lately that's three.js, Godot
      and plain old C, plus slowly teaching myself the math I never quite got
      the first time around.
    </p>
    <p>
      Away from the keyboard I'm usually out mountain biking, daydreaming about
      turning a van into a home on wheels, or taking photos with my Fujifilm.
      The ones I'm proud of end up on
      <Link href="https://kevinthebard.com">kevinthebard.com</Link>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
